Created the base pipeline in order to add and store files in webm files. It first prompts for you to add a file in its local folder, then prompts you to add a video file into it. It then asks for the output video name and confirms the process (and ensures that the output is in webm format). It then reads the webm video bytes to identify how far away the ZIP file needs to be placed (as webm files don't read data beyond the video). It them creates a temporary virtual file inside of ram, and opens a compressor that writes into that ram. It then walks through the directory to find the file (or files) and writes it, converting the bytes of the ZIP file to an array. For verification it checks the end of the ZIP byte data to find the 4 byte signature. It then grabs the ZIP metadata (bit numbers are found from the PKWARE APPNOTE spec) converts it into human readable text and saves it as a variable so when it needs to be extracted it knows where to look.
